# Transformation identity

The transformation identity should include, at minimum:

```text
specification schema version
source relation identity
source key fields and ordering
source input fields and ordering
source filters or scope
preprocessing configuration
Unicode normalization, if any
whitespace handling
field concatenation semantics
empty-input policy
truncation policy
maximum input size
model provider type
endpoint class
model identifier
model revision or digest where available
requested output dimension where supported
reported output dimension
normalization policy
pooling or encoding options where configurable
distance metric
target representation
target generation identity
Ptah operation-contract version
```

The following must change generation identity:

* source field set;
* source field order;
* preprocessing;
* truncation;
* model;
* model revision;
* output dimension;
* normalization;
* distance metric;
* target vector representation.

The generation identity should not include:

* transient provider request IDs;
* timestamps;
* worker count;
* retry count;
* display name;
* mutable OCI tag;
* mutable model alias without its resolved identity.

When a provider does not expose an immutable model revision, Ptah must record:

```text
reproducibility = partial
```

and explain why.

It must not fabricate an immutable identity.

