# Embedding provider architecture

The embedding provider contract is separate from Ptah Assist's conversational provider contract.

They may share low-level credential, proxy, TLS, and HTTP utilities where appropriate.

They must not be conflated semantically.

## Required provider behavior

A provider adapter should represent:

```text
provider identity
endpoint class
base URL
credential reference
model identifier
model revision where available
batch support
maximum batch size
maximum input size
requested output dimension where supported
reported output dimension
normalization behavior
timeout policy
retry metadata
rate-limit metadata
usage metadata
request identity
```

## Initial provider

The first implementation should support a deliberately scoped OpenAI-compatible embedding API.

"Compatible" must mean behavior tested against a documented adapter contract.

It must not imply every server accepting a similar URL is supported.

## Local endpoints

Local and self-hosted endpoints are first-class architecture requirements.

A local endpoint may omit credentials.

Ptah should still record:

* endpoint class;
* model identity;
* reachability;
* capability result;
* tested or untested status.

## Provider test

A provider-profile test must verify without sending repository or source-row content:

* endpoint reachability;
* authentication;
* selected model reachability;
* embedding operation support;
* batch behavior;
* output shape;
* output dimension;
* finite numeric output;
* cancellation;
* representative error normalization.

## No silent fallback

If the selected provider fails, Ptah must not send source content to another provider automatically.

Any fallback system is out of scope until it can be:

* explicitly configured;
* visible;
* privacy-reviewed;
* identity-preserving or identity-changing in an explicit way;
* audited per request.

## Credentials

Credentials are references, not values.

Candidate sources:

```text
env:
keychain:
credential-helper:
file: with strict permission checks
Kubernetes Secret reference
workload identity
```

Keys must not appear in:

* project configuration values;
* process arguments;
* logs;
* state tables;
* reports;
* MCP resources;
* Assist messages;
* session exports;
* OCI artifacts.

## Provider-bound content manifest

Before execution, Ptah should be able to report:

* which source columns are selected;
* whether the endpoint is local or remote;
* provider profile name;
* endpoint host class, without credentials;
* preprocessing and truncation policy;
* approximate row count where known;
* maximum bytes per request;
* whether raw content is retained by Ptah;
* whether provider retention is controlled outside Ptah.

Ptah must not claim provider-side no-retention guarantees it cannot enforce.

## Response validation

Every response must be checked for:

* one output per accepted input;
* stable result association;
* expected dimension;
* finite values;
* no `NaN`;
* no positive or negative infinity;
* maximum serialized size;
* provider error inside a nominal success response;
* cancellation and partial-stream behavior where applicable.

A partial batch response must not be marked complete.

