Definition of done

This issue is complete when a backend or platform engineer who has not worked on the inference implementation can:

1. discover the feature from the main documentation;
2. explain what Ptah manages and what it does not manage;
3. select a consistency mode for a static or live source;
4. write a valid inference specification;
5. execute the complete lifecycle in a local environment;
6. understand why backfill completion alone is insufficient;
7. interpret verification and consistency blockers;
8. recover a failed or interrupted run;
9. perform a safe cutover;
10. determine whether rollback is still possible;
11. retire an old generation without confusing retirement with rollback.

The result must be a user documentation system, not a prose copy of #2068 or #2354.
